            <h2>What is Midjourney?</h2>

            <p>Midjourney is an AI image generator that runs entirely through Discord. Founded by David Holz (former Leap Motion founder), it launched in July 2022 and quickly became the gold standard for AI-generated art.</p>

            <p>Unlike DALL-E 3 (integrated into ChatGPT) or Stable Diffusion (open-source software), Midjourney operates as a <strong>Discord bot</strong>. You type commands like <code>/imagine prompt: a serene mountain landscape at sunset</code> and Midjourney generates four image variations in 30-60 seconds.</p>

            <h3>Key Stats (2026):</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>20+ million users</strong> worldwide</li>
                <li><strong>V6 model</strong> (released late 2023, refined through 2024-2025)</li>
                <li><strong>Discord-only interface</strong> (no web app, mobile via Discord app)</li>
                <li><strong>Pricing:</strong> $10/month (Basic), $30/month (Standard), $60/month (Pro), $120/month (Mega)</li>
                <li><strong>Commercial use:</strong> Allowed on paid plans</li>
                <li><strong>No free tier</strong> (ended in 2023 due to abuse)</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Midjourney V6: What's New in 2026</h2>

            <p>Midjourney V6, the current flagship model, represents a massive leap over V5. Here's what improved:</p>

            <h3>V6 Improvements:</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Photorealism:</strong> V6 can generate near-photographic images when prompted correctly</li>
                <li><strong>Prompt adherence:</strong> Better understanding of detailed, longer prompts (up to ~350 words)</li>
                <li><strong>Text rendering:</strong> Improved but still not perfect (Ideogram beats it here)</li>
                <li><strong>Anatomy & hands:</strong> Significantly better human anatomy and hand rendering</li>
                <li><strong>Coherence:</strong> More consistent style across upscaled and varied images</li>
                <li><strong>Aspect ratios:</strong> Support for custom aspect ratios beyond standard 16:9, 1:1, etc.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>V6 also introduced <strong>style references</strong> (--sref) and <strong>character references</strong> (--cref), allowing you to maintain consistent styles or characters across generations.</p>

