            <h2>Detailed Feature Breakdown</h2>

            <h3>1. Image Quality & Artistic Style</h3>
            <p><strong>Winner: Midjourney</strong></p>

            <p>Midjourney's defining characteristic is <strong>consistent artistic excellence</strong>. Even simple prompts produce aesthetically pleasing results. The model has a natural bias toward:</p>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>Cinematic lighting:</strong> Dramatic, professionally lit scenes</li>
                <li><strong>Rich color palettes:</strong> Vibrant yet balanced color choices</li>
                <li><strong>Artistic composition:</strong> Rule of thirds, leading lines, depth</li>
                <li><strong>Texture detail:</strong> Impressive surface detail and materials</li>
            </ul>

            <p>This makes Midjourney ideal for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Concept art for games, films, books</li>
                <li>Marketing visuals and hero images</li>
                <li>Book covers and editorial illustrations</li>
                <li>Social media content that needs to "pop"</li>
                <li>Fine art prints and gallery work</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>2. Discord-Based Workflow</h3>
            <p><strong>Unique to Midjourney (Pro/Con)</strong></p>

            <p>Midjourney's Discord-only interface is controversial. Here's the reality:</p>

            <p><strong>Why Discord:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Community exposure:</strong> See what others are creating, learn from their prompts</li>
                <li><strong>Rapid iteration:</strong> Discord's speed suits fast experimentation</li>
                <li><strong>Social learning:</strong> Public channels teach prompt engineering through observation</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Discord Downsides:</strong></p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Learning curve:</strong> Memorizing slash commands (/imagine, /blend, /describe, etc.)</li>
                <li><strong>No traditional interface:</strong> No drag-and-drop, no visual editor</li>
                <li><strong>Image management:</strong> Finding old generations requires scrolling through Discord history</li>
                <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> Generations are public by default (private mode requires Pro plan or higher)</li>
            </ul>

            <p><strong>Workaround:</strong> Use Direct Messages with the Midjourney Bot for private generation, or upgrade to a plan with Stealth Mode ($60/month Pro plan).</p>

            <h3>3. Prompt Control & Parameters</h3>
            <p><strong>Advanced but learnable</strong></p>

            <p>Midjourney uses parameters to control output. Key parameters include:</p>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>--ar (aspect ratio):</strong> <code>--ar 16:9</code>, <code>--ar 1:1</code>, <code>--ar 3:2</code></li>
                <li><strong>--s (stylize):</strong> How "artistic" vs literal (0-1000, default 100)</li>
                <li><strong>--v (version):</strong> <code>--v 6</code> for V6, <code>--v 5.2</code> for V5.2, etc.</li>
                <li><strong>--chaos:</strong> Variation randomness (0-100)</li>
                <li><strong>--weird:</strong> Unconventional, experimental results (0-3000)</li>
                <li><strong>--sref (style reference):</strong> Match a reference image's style</li>
                <li><strong>--cref (character reference):</strong> Maintain consistent characters</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Example prompt: <code>/imagine a cyberpunk street market at night, neon lights, rain --ar 16:9 --s 750 --v 6</code></p>

            <h3>4. V6 Photorealism & Accuracy</h3>
            <p><strong>Dramatically improved in V6</strong></p>

            <p>V6 introduced photorealistic capabilities. To trigger photorealism:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Use descriptive, detailed prompts (like DALL-E 3)</li>
                <li>Specify photography terms: "shot on Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.4, natural lighting"</li>
                <li>Lower stylization: <code>--s 0</code> to <code>--s 250</code></li>
            </ul>

            <p>V6 photorealism rivals DALL-E 3 but retains Midjourney's artistic flair even in realistic modes.</p>

            <h3>5. Upscaling & Variations</h3>
            <p><strong>Flexible iteration workflow</strong></p>

            <p>Midjourney generates 4 variations per prompt. From there:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>U1-U4 buttons:</strong> Upscale (increase resolution) any of the 4 images</li>
                <li><strong>V1-V4 buttons:</strong> Create 4 new variations similar to chosen image</li>
                <li><strong>Vary (Strong/Subtle):</strong> V6 feature for controlled variations</li>
                <li><strong>Zoom Out:</strong> Expand the image canvas</li>
                <li><strong>Pan arrows:</strong> Extend image in specific directions</li>
            </ul>

            <p>This workflow encourages exploration and iteration.</p>

