            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <h3>Can I use Midjourney images commercially?</h3>
            <p>Yes! All paid plans (Basic, Standard, Pro, Mega) include commercial use rights. You own the images you generate (subject to Midjourney's Terms of Service). This makes it viable for client work, products, and sales.</p>

            <h3>Is there a Midjourney free trial or free tier?</h3>
            <p>No. Midjourney discontinued free trials in March 2023 due to abuse. The cheapest option is the Basic plan at $10/month. However, you can cancel anytime, so try it for one month risk-free.</p>

            <h3>Can I use Midjourney without Discord?</h3>
            <p>No. Midjourney is Discord-only. There's been speculation about a web interface, but as of December 2026, Discord is the only way to access Midjourney. You can use Discord's mobile app for on-the-go generation.</p>

            <h3>How does Midjourney V6 compare to DALL-E 3?</h3>
            <p>Midjourney V6 produces more consistently artistic, visually stunning images. DALL-E 3 is better at understanding complex natural language prompts and has better text rendering. DALL-E 3 is easier to use (integrated into ChatGPT), while Midjourney requires learning Discord commands. Quality-wise, they're comparable, with Midjourney having a slight edge on pure aesthetics.</p>

            <h3>What's the difference between Fast and Relax mode?</h3>
            <p>Fast Mode uses dedicated GPU resources and generates images in ~60 seconds. It consumes your monthly GPU hours (3.3 hrs on Basic, 15 hrs on Standard, etc.). Relax Mode is unlimited but queued—images take 5-10 minutes depending on server load. Relax is only available on Standard, Pro, and Mega plans.</p>

            <h3>Can I get private/stealth generation on Midjourney?</h3>
            <p>Yes, but only with the Pro plan ($60/month) or Mega plan ($120/month). These include Stealth Mode, which makes your generations invisible to other users. On Basic and Standard plans, your images are public in community feeds (though you can DM the bot for semi-privacy).</p>

            <h3>Does Midjourney have an API?</h3>
            <p>No. Midjourney does not offer a public API as of December 2026. If you need programmatic image generation, use DALL-E 3 (via OpenAI API), Stable Diffusion (via Stability AI API or self-hosted), or Ideogram (limited API in beta).</p>

